# A plan whose gate criterion POOLS lifetime history cannot be reached by adding more days — the October arming plan was arithmetically unreachable under its own gate

## Symptom

`FABLE-FULL-AUDIT-2026-09-01.md` line 12: "the plan to arm real money in October is
arithmetically unreachable under the frozen config." Gate criterion 1 (statistics) was RED
on all 4 arms (CI-lower 0.33-0.41 vs the 1.0 bar) and re-scoring it every night between
09-01 and October could not have fixed it — to turn the gate green by 09-29, safe-2 would
have needed +$166/day for 19 straight sessions against an actual run-rate of -$7/day; the
best arm (risky-1) needed +$115/day against an actual +$50/day.

## Root cause

Criterion 1 is defined over an arm's ENTIRE lifetime fill history, not a bounded recent
window. A plan that says "wait N more days and re-check the gate" implicitly assumes the
gate's denominator is the window you're adding days to — but a lifetime-pooled bootstrap
CI dilutes new days into an ever-growing history at a rate that new days alone cannot move
fast enough to cross a fixed CI-lower bar in any realistic calendar. The plan's authors
treated "more trading days" and "gate criterion improves" as the same lever; they are not,
once the criterion's scope is lifetime rather than windowed.

## Fix

Commit `04f80c3f` (2026-09-01): `go_live_gate.py` criterion 5 wired to a new
`automation/state/prod-shadow-designation.json` (currently designating `safe-3`, frozen
window `2026-09-01..2026-10-30`, `min_days: 20`). Criterion 5 — a bounded prod-shadow
window on the DESIGNATED profile — becomes the actual arming bar; criterion 1 (lifetime
robustness) is reframed as a DISCLOSURE, not a bar (see work order §0 decision 1, RULE9-
DOC-PASS-2026-09-05-DRAFT.md item 1's CLAUDE.md rewrite of the Live-threshold line).

## Generalizable pattern

Before writing "ship if X clears the gate by date D," check what WINDOW the gate's metric
is actually computed over. A gate scoped to "since inception" or "all fills ever" cannot be
budged meaningfully by N additional days once the history is large enough — the fix is
either a rolling/bounded window (what shipped here) or an explicit acknowledgment that the
plan is waiting on something else (a parameter change, a regime shift) rather than on time
passing. Sibling to C4 (normalize OOS, disclose concentration) — this is the same failure
in the other direction: an aggregate metric masking that "more data" cannot move it.
